preloader-stock.img

This file is Miyoo vendor firmware: the stock SPI preloader (DDR init and SPL),
2 MiB. The Zlyme script in this package is MIT. That license does not cover
this image.

Source repository:
  Zetarancio/Miyoo-Flip-Mainline-Linux-Reverse-Engineering
Pinned wiki commit:
  c126d3235face9ddca5bf021258a84758dca543c
Source path:
  preloader-stock-rocknix/App/apommel-multiboot/preloader-stock.img
Introducing commit:
  8ef495f5711ce13645e9c68df63b7d7a9934cf7e
SHA-256:
  dfdd7d20d6fd3beb18350dcf8fa58740b40b4baaf39467d45076f949053a2922
Historical MD5:
  1d525e6e6c89bd788b5245c90c97833b

The wiki documents this image as byte-identical to the first 2 MiB of
spi_20241119160817.img. It also documents that more than one stock SPL build
exists, so this file is not a universal stock preloader.

Known patched counterpart, fingerprint only. That file is not installed:
  preloader-stock-rocknix/App/apommel-multiboot/preloader-patched.img
  SHA-256 ed10591f62ae0b8845ac9bd6cf80c896a2b172d32c7c4ef6564d305e8662c13d
  Historical MD5 c2009762b1704d5ed2ebbfa4346e6ecc

zlyme-preloader may write this image only when no per-device
mtd5-original-<sha256>.img exists and the installed preloader matches that
patched fingerprint, and only after the usual structure and DDR checks.

Redistribution: the wiki records where the bytes came from. It does not
contain a license, a copyright grant, or permission from Miyoo to
redistribute this preloader. A sentence in the wiki calls a shared DRAM blob
technically redistributable because it matches public rkbin and other units.
That is not a license for this image. Do not treat a public Zlyme release as
cleared to ship it until that grant exists.
